<%# A CATEGORY THAT BEHAVES LIKE A RATE AND IS FUNDED BY NOTHING. Local: `suggestion`.

    §8's copy target: `Coffee — $35 a period for 6 months, currently comes out of your buffer`.
    The "out of your buffer" half is the reason the suggestion exists at all — the category has no
    pool, so nothing reserves this money and every dollar of it lands on whatever is left over.

    THE DIVISOR IS NAMED. `amount` is the observed total divided by the periods the category has
    been ALIVE for, not by the periods it appeared in (a per-occurrence figure proposed as a rate
    over-reserves by window ÷ appearances — the engine's first correction), so the sentence says
    both counts: how many periods it showed up in, and how many it was averaged over. %>
<p>
  <span class="font-medium text-gray-900"><%= suggestion.subject.name %></span> —
  <span class="tabular-nums"><%= number_to_currency(suggestion.amount) %></span> a period,
  currently comes out of your buffer.
</p>

<p class="text-gray-500">
  <%= number_to_currency(suggestion.detail[:observed_total]) %> spent in
  <%= suggestion.detail[:periods_present] %> of the last <%= suggestion.detail[:periods_window] %> periods,
  first on <%= suggestion.detail[:first_seen_on].strftime("%b %-d, %Y") %>, averaged over
  <%= pluralize(suggestion.detail[:periods_measured], "period") %>.
</p>
